-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Foundations.Introspection.RegisterEPR` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). # Splitting the maximally entangled state along computational registers
--
--   Extending a local operator by identity on complementary EPR coordinates costs no error.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open MIPRE
--   open MIPRE.Introspection
--   open Finset Matrix Classical
--   open scoped Kronecker
--   variable {I J R H K : Type*}
--
--   theorem MIPRE.Introspection.stateSqNorm_registerExtend [Nonempty R] (e : I ≃ J × R)
--       (ξ : H × K → ℂ) (M : Matrix (J × H) (J × H) ℂ) :
--       stateSqNorm (registerState I ξ) (registerExtend e M) =
--         stateSqNorm (registerState J ξ) M
--   ```
--
--   **Formalization Note** `MIPRE.Introspection.stateSqNorm_registerExtend` is declared in `MIPRE/Foundations/Introspection/RegisterEPR.lean`, lines 125–143. The binders, hypotheses and conclusion are exactly those of the Lean statement above; the uploaded statement elaborates to the same type as the declaration in the repository. The definitions it mentions are those of the published definition bundles of the module's import closure.
